    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63823dcf_99683ffa",
        "filename": "Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-11T05:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just added the requested comments. \n\nBased on Chisato\u0027s comment, the ARM Cortex-R series and certain external 32-bit DSPs do not have FPU and would need this flag enabled. \n\nI looked at code in build/soong/cc/config/arm_device.go, it seems that only the following ARM variants are being considered by Soong:\n\t\t\"armv5te\",\n\t\t\"armv7_a\",\n\t\t\"armv7_a_neon\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a7\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a8\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a9\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a15\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a53\",\n\t\t\"cortex_a53_a57\",\n\t\t\"krait\",\n\t\t\"denver\"\n\nIt seems that all of these variants have FPUs on-board (ARM-VFP). In the future, if we do encounter devices that meet Chisato\u0027s description, we should add that architecture support in Soong and add the cflag through the \"arch\" clause such as\n\narch: {\n  cortex_r4: {\n    cflags: [\"-D_32BIT_FIXED_POINT\"],\n  }\n}\n\ninstead of a custom Makefile flag.",
      "parentUuid": "63823dcf_f6b940d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 20
      },
